{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:06Z","created_by_operation":"op_1d447a6b36934b63b8140cfb78fe8578","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_bf6fad0bc01259d9e7174ae92c30d1d157d85f2346bbdbf034d8236f23aa9c6a","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"getkimchi/kimchi@15cdadae0c44 snapshot 2a86d2323cfc7801","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5ba23c5cbaa5a172cd15a827f3e598fd42bcb25513fddd705400bb3a42ec8488","slc_78d47ca2fe7c65eae490466d305447d8271c3d1f849ad9175deffa1c4b577164","slc_c7e0a43daabbe1e03ce97c293154ef1d189e2b44128cec720db202352aa7a03f","slc_ca25cbc8b62e0e6016bf5db2e4abbc86f38f1c144bf04785e07f9b377f3f63d8","slc_eb63a3597b7f472bd343409c81a54b36504d9f728efcc6561aebc3867828f9a5"],"source_ids":["src_0f6cf79ec69e5941857254efb708262f"],"text":"Ferment lifecycle follows a deterministic state machine (draft, planned, running, paused, complete) that rejects illegal transitions, with manual or automated continuation policies and pause/resume/exit commands.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:06Z","updated_by_operation":"op_1d447a6b36934b63b8140cfb78fe8578"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:06Z","created_by_operation":"op_1d447a6b36934b63b8140cfb78fe8578","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_c5e984f49570ac9e2b5f68e6d97faffa993a95f5ca4c742d6072da77f8f2fd93","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"getkimchi/kimchi@15cdadae0c44 snapshot 2a86d2323cfc7801","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_34db1b92fac70085d92e67a5330cafd1f5f1bf58c585c50bcc5f23b6a554e14c","slc_8a9982905806b25c092d9dc391d978a270aee1264a3002e3ba35f98d59355701","slc_ee80736e2844dc00556ef5c67bf83300b2b1fb1e544fed60795300aedfb62b7a"],"source_ids":["src_0f6cf79ec69e5941857254efb708262f"],"text":"On first run kimchi detects Claude Code, OpenCode, or Cursor installations and offers one-shot migration of their MCP servers and skills, merging discovered servers into `~/.config/kimchi/harness/mcp.json` with existing Kimchi entries winning collisions.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:06Z","updated_by_operation":"op_1d447a6b36934b63b8140cfb78fe8578"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:06Z","created_by_operation":"op_1d447a6b36934b63b8140cfb78fe8578","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_de74f4c4b6cd1d846eb411ab5ab7dd8aab46f486e03d44fb508e7845ffcb8262","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"getkimchi/kimchi@15cdadae0c44 snapshot 2a86d2323cfc7801","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_9d02527c1621ccfcd44b94e4bb716240e13866dfdd33a5a8b44a9d76fd082037","slc_f9834bbaeae18cfef4bf191f2cd0ba09ae7e6a3181569d55d8e6aeacb3a206ba"],"source_ids":["src_0f6cf79ec69e5941857254efb708262f"],"text":"Kimchi runs in single-model or multi-model mode; in multi-model mode an orchestrator delegates each task to a model assigned to a role, while single-model mode disables task classification and delegation but keeps the orchestration system prompt.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:06Z","updated_by_operation":"op_1d447a6b36934b63b8140cfb78fe8578"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:06Z","created_by_operation":"op_1d447a6b36934b63b8140cfb78fe8578","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_dfec68178a83d7cdf7565c9d8b574b7361993e10e73c7ec422be797b0cff78e0","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"getkimchi/kimchi@15cdadae0c44 snapshot 2a86d2323cfc7801","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2663f8f6ecac2b77877543655f31ac3229c638ba550df7023063a5c25882ade4"],"source_ids":["src_0f6cf79ec69e5941857254efb708262f"],"text":"Users can add Bash hooks that rewrite or block shell commands before execution; global hooks live in `~/.config/kimchi/harness/hooks/bash/` and project hooks in `.kimchi/hooks/bash/` default to disabled until enabled.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:06Z","updated_by_operation":"op_1d447a6b36934b63b8140cfb78fe8578"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:06Z","created_by_operation":"op_1d447a6b36934b63b8140cfb78fe8578","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_e2afac5e91e1a7dce409df6fea74b0fc644c7b4b691c42ed450a43c19d9b5948","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"getkimchi/kimchi@15cdadae0c44 snapshot 2a86d2323cfc7801","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4439a27b1604d08ff0cfe20fe335f22848a542481d015570e83a26eef9521b81","slc_6bc6ce42416b66a9bd057f241dd5c00a06bf6cc794bffb3b71a7d48dfde694d9","slc_9ad401803c1525fac875b26aedd3edeb81eff50f76bd9d2cf82f403a97c1e730","slc_cfbe30b77d0edcfb6dda0e99213be3fea41a05368e200b645a62c909993aec71"],"source_ids":["src_0f6cf79ec69e5941857254efb708262f"],"text":"Ferment V2 is an experimental, branch-scoped objective controller (disabled by default, enabled under /resources) that keeps one objective across turns, supports token budgets, and evaluates completion with an independent tool-free evaluator returning met, impossible, or continue.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:06Z","updated_by_operation":"op_1d447a6b36934b63b8140cfb78fe8578"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:06Z","created_by_operation":"op_1d447a6b36934b63b8140cfb78fe8578","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_f6baf63463890ec776c5542ba9b98c7283da1e7b90d412c68ce7a1921b687360","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"getkimchi/kimchi@15cdadae0c44 snapshot 2a86d2323cfc7801","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_54c9da3cd515678233753c9ea921efa62d410051b97c3bf31886b904cace8f79","slc_d2a2cccbb1cdb6aa10cb8830c236d1635186e5d05e69099a01d14a48d8e9be5c","slc_d5d15da4ab1959871b50837d05192a5ebb1ae3aaef6165393405944950f14fb9","slc_d64baf08856d3e08dd6e82bf67c0da4c8d182a80969e2f4360ba7a5458ab3cf3"],"source_ids":["src_0f6cf79ec69e5941857254efb708262f"],"text":"Every LLM request is tagged with a `phase:{name}` label (explore, plan, build, review, research) for usage analytics and cost attribution; subagents inherit the phase but cannot change it, and user tags persist with the session.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:06Z","updated_by_operation":"op_1d447a6b36934b63b8140cfb78fe8578"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:06Z","created_by_operation":"op_1d447a6b36934b63b8140cfb78fe8578","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_facf28b1ae8f5d4cc12f47b17ce63ec00626314bbbad22d3b4664a0642742b3c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"getkimchi/kimchi@15cdadae0c44 snapshot 2a86d2323cfc7801","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_19fe86f5daf5953d89a7c473993ec64acf8a692637e5f160756ea703724d7555","slc_c40a30ffd46c8188b211a810e7be732b13d23953a0ec0458e987b0a4bd25cfe3","slc_e0294d7a7be8ca92070556aee52128937ea1f7b0aa17d5840168a73679198529","slc_ef895989878da83cface3cc7b3f8ec8ef9dcae99548d9350b46a768cc3fe911f"],"source_ids":["src_0f6cf79ec69e5941857254efb708262f"],"text":"Ferment persists project state (goal, phases, steps, decisions, memory) as a JSON snapshot plus an append-only events log under `.kimchi/ferments/`, with every mutation hashed for auditability, and sessions resume from a `ferment_reference` entry in the session log.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:06Z","updated_by_operation":"op_1d447a6b36934b63b8140cfb78fe8578"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:06Z","created_by_operation":"op_1d447a6b36934b63b8140cfb78fe8578","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_fff98665c7fd85a916b6deab85323d6378b08dad5dcdbd71d671a1805b72ca9b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"getkimchi/kimchi@15cdadae0c44 snapshot 2a86d2323cfc7801","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_659cc1c56b90e2e9444235720685a29ea986f8e2731859aba1cf7c0523c8f01b","slc_923744550188e7b2eb9eb3fef8ca5d975fd6d43ae14acbd311edd5df2d8b484f"],"source_ids":["src_0f6cf79ec69e5941857254efb708262f"],"text":"The orchestrator receives per-phase directives: it performs work for roles it owns, delegates otherwise, and review is always delegated to a fresh context for independence.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:51:06Z","updated_by_operation":"op_1d447a6b36934b63b8140cfb78fe8578"}
